It might be useful to list the ways in which Lojban fails to meet human lan=
guage standards.  I personally can't think of one (even xorlo has, alas, hu=
man analogs).  Remember that at least one school of linguists think that al=
l sentences in any natural language are merely transforms of predicate logi=
c sentences, with minor loss of information.




